WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.690
<b>[Urgent]
 Sales Department One: 
Dealing With Miyazumi Tatsuru 

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:05.150
Now everything is in place.

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:09.090
He managed to cause a problem 
at exactly the right time for us.

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:13.260
Disbanding the badminton team is essential 
to slimming down the sales department.

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:18.950
And the first step toward 
doing that is firing Miyazumi.

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:23.870
What is the old man doing?

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:26.410
This is an important match for us.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:28.930
Coach.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.690
One of our team members is late.

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:33.300
Wait, what's with the suit?

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.970
Tatsu probably won't make 
it in time for the match.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:37.180
Huh?

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:40.390
He's been called into the office.

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:42.070
Tatsu-san's been called in?!

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:43.350
What happened?

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:44.980
What about the semifinals?!

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:46.440
Shut up!

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.810
I'm confirming the situation.

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:51.570
You boys focus on the match in front of you.

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:55.390
Saeki brothers and Usuyama, get warmed up.

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:59.160
Shiratori, worst case, 
you'll play with Takeda.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:00.740
Wha... Me?

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:29.270
<b><i>Salaryman's Club</i></b>

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:38.220
The subject of today's 
emergency board meeting

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:42.470
is how we'll deal with Miyazumi-kun, 
who has committed an act of violence.

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:42.470
<b><i>#10: Tradeoff</i></b>

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:44.740
What? Violence?

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:48.180
The other day, we held a dinner 
with Vice President Tokui,

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:51.430
son of the president of 
izakaya chain Toku-chan.

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:54.130
At that dinner, you committed 
an act of violence.

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:55.800
Am I wrong?

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:58.980
I don't remember committing 
any acts of violence—

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:00.610
Don't lie to me!

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:03.540
The vice president is, in fact, injured!

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:06.490
He suddenly pushed me.

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:10.050
You tripped on your own.

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:12.210
Sir, you were there, too.

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:14.570
I did indeed witness the 
incident with my own eyes.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:16.920
You pushed him.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:19.860
Oshitari-kun,

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:22.580
surely we don't need to do this on
 the day of an important tournament.

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:25.700
Allowing the culprit in such a scandal to

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:29.060
participate in a tournament would 
damage people's faith in our company.

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:32.270
I believe it would be appropriate 
to have Miyazumi-kun stay home

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:36.270
and consider his future at 
the company during this time.

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:38.230
But...

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:42.080
Are you telling me to quit?

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:46.220
Why isn't he even reading my messages?

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:47.650
Shiratori-kun!

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:49.220
What am I gonna do?!

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:52.160
I tried talking to the executive 
director, but he wouldn't listen!

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:53.870
Y-Yata-san?

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:57.340
Calm down. What happened?

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:02.930
The other day, Miyazumi-san and I accompanied 
the executive director to a dinner.

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:05.930
Meat and red wine are a match made in heaven.

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:09.760
Do you understand the 
pairing of wine and meat?

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:13.290
Most impressive, Vice President 
Tokui. You're so knowledgeable!

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:15.120
Give it a taste.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:18.320
Actually, uh, I'm not too fond of wine.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:21.670
It's all right. This one's very drinkable.

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:27.160
Hey, you're right! I could 
drink a whole mug of this.

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:34.580
A friend of mine runs a bar around here.

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:35.670
Why don't we go check it out?

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:37.030
Uh...

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:40.190
They've got great drinks and finger food.

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:42.260
Seriously? That sounds great!

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:44.670
Just how inconsiderate are you?!

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:45.680
What's your problem?!

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:50.060
It's all right. I can go all night long.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:52.870
Shut up! What's wrong with you?

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:03.900
Sir!

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:07.210
And now they're saying it
 was an act of violence.

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:11.540
What... What am I going to do 
if Miyazumi-san is fired?!

00:05:13.570 --> 00:05:15.000
I'll do something about it.

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:15.960
Huh?

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:26.780
Think we can win?

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:28.390
Tatsuru-san's not here.

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:30.310
We have to step up.

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:32.210
Yeah.

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:36.730
Sir, don't you think demanding 
his resignation is a bit much?

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:40.040
I'm just asking him to consider it.

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:42.690
I won't accept this! We need 
to confirm the facts—

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:44.560
You're awfully persistent, aren't you?

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:47.530
People who have done 
wrong always deny it.

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:50.950
It also sounds like in 
addition to this incident,

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:53.490
Miyazumi-kun has all sorts of other problems.

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:54.800
Exactly!

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:58.050
At the tasting in June,

00:05:58.050 --> 00:06:01.290
he used a transport company with whom we 
had no contract without authorization.

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:06.260
His deviation from the rules 
cannot be overlooked!

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:11.100
He's just adjusting to circumstances 
for the sake of our clients.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:13.390
They speak very highly of them.

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:16.810
We also seem to have some employees 
who aren't too happy with him.

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:21.980
His sudden orders increase 
the amount of unscheduled work.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:24.000
He spends too much entertaining clients.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:26.860
Even a quick investigation turned up
 a lot of complaints about you.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:30.740
But those have nothing 
to do with this incident.

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:35.700
Don't you think allowing this problematic 
behavior to continue emboldened him?

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:41.830
I do think there were aspects of my behavior 
that may have been a little pushy.

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:43.250
I'll correct that, going forward.

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:47.010
But I swear I never committed 
any violent acts.

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:50.300
I see. I understand.

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:53.470
If you're so insistent you 
didn't, then I'll believe you.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:58.680
But in exchange, the badminton 
team will be disbanded.

00:06:59.130 --> 00:06:59.810
What?

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.570
<b>Saeki Sota 
Saeki Toya</b>

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:07.570
I'm surprised.

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:12.360
You're playing doubles, Sota. Not only that, 
but you're playing with your brother.

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:16.830
What a shame. I was prepared to
 play against Miyazumi and Shiratori.

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:29.420
Damn.

00:07:29.690 --> 00:07:31.530
So this is how large the 
gap is between them.

00:07:31.530 --> 00:07:34.250
No, they'll still get their chance.

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:44.100
They're so strong.

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:49.840
This is the world's second-ranked team.

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:52.780
Hold on.

00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:56.350
The badminton team has 
nothing to do with this.

00:07:56.350 --> 00:08:00.590
A team whose member has caused 
a scandal can't be allowed to operate.

00:08:00.590 --> 00:08:03.120
If people learned someone like 
that was the team captain,

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:05.830
it would destroy our company's image.

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:10.930
Plus, I've been questioning the necessity of
 the badminton team for some time now.

00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:14.800
We receive very little in return 
for the cost of maintaining it.

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:20.030
We should use those funds elsewhere to 
expand our business, increase profits,

00:08:20.030 --> 00:08:21.850
and give back to our employees!

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:25.400
Is that not how a company should operate?!

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:28.460
The team should be shut down!

00:08:28.460 --> 00:08:29.730
But...

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:33.410
Because you won't admit 
fault, we have no choice.

00:08:33.410 --> 00:08:35.360
You're being held collectively responsible.

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:42.680
If I quit the company, will the badminton 
team be allowed to continue to operate?

00:08:42.680 --> 00:08:46.040
That depends on your attitude.

00:08:49.270 --> 00:08:50.710
Very well.

00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:58.950
As of today, I, Miyazumi Tatsuru 
of Sunlight Beverage...

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:04.180
Shiratori?

00:09:06.450 --> 00:09:07.510
Mikoto?

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:12.070
<b>Kirishima Hayato
 Oginome Daiki</b>

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:12.070
<b>Saeki Sota
 Saeki Toya</b>

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:15.800
Game two has been nothing but 
a defensive battle so far, too.

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:18.780
Damn it. If only they could find their form...

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:27.370
<i>There it is!</i>

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:31.630
<i>He moved up?</i>

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:32.840
<i>Now.</i>

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:35.800
<i>What?!</i>

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:39.510
All right! They did it!

00:09:40.690 --> 00:09:41.700
What's wrong?

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:43.840
Their front player was blocking the shuttle.

00:09:43.840 --> 00:09:46.020
Can't help that, then. 
Let's get the next one.

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:02.870
<i>Start with a jab.</i>

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:10.130
Ow!

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:14.090
Sorry, Bro.

00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:20.930
It's not on purpose, really.

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:27.060
<i>That's odd. It's like the shuttle is being 
sucked in toward my brother's head.</i>

00:10:28.780 --> 00:10:29.260
Huh?

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:33.540
Nice, Sota!

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:39.300
That's it!

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:41.690
<b>Saeki Sota 
Saeki Toya</b>

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:41.700
<b>Kirishima Hayato
 Oginome Daiki</b>

00:10:47.060 --> 00:10:50.920
<i>They're deliberately hiding their 
smashes behind their front player.</i>

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:56.380
<i>We won't keep falling for the same trick.</i>

00:10:57.210 --> 00:10:59.510
<i>We can handle it when we know it's coming.</i>

00:11:03.590 --> 00:11:05.410
Let's play like we always do.

00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:07.140
Once we're used to it, 
there's no need to panic.

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:08.520
Yeah.

00:11:08.790 --> 00:11:11.400
<i>We expected them to figure 
out how to handle it.</i>

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:12.730
<i>The real battle starts here.</i>

00:11:15.220 --> 00:11:16.000
Here it comes.

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:22.910
14-11.

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:25.330
A net-cord.

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:27.620
It was a lucky shot. Don't let it bother you.

00:11:34.470 --> 00:11:36.670
<i>Is he doing it on purpose?</i>

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:42.260
<i>Is that even possible?</i>

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:47.720
The huge by-product of all their 
training is that net-cord smash.

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:49.930
<b>Kirishima Hayato
 Oginome Daiki</b>

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:49.930
<b>Saeki Sota
 Saeki Toya</b>

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:57.480
For some reason, he can't do it 
without Sota's head in front of him.

00:11:58.290 --> 00:12:00.190
Only the Saeki brothers can pull this off.

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:08.950
<b>Kirishima Hayato
 Oginome Daiki</b>

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:08.950
<b>Saeki Sota
 Saeki Toya</b>

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:10.730
Yes!

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:15.580
You again?

00:12:16.430 --> 00:12:17.880
Wait, Mikoto.

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:27.990
Ow...

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:33.140
What do you think you're doing, 
 and why didn't you tell anyone?

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:38.650
Wh-What am <i>I</i> doing? What are <i>you</i> 
doing?! What about the match?!

00:12:38.890 --> 00:12:41.030
The others will win.

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:44.700
So I'm here to do what I can.

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:50.500
The badminton team needs Miyazumi-san.

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:54.660
I learned to do my job because of this man.

00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:58.380
I learned to play badminton properly 
because he teamed up with me!

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:00.370
Mikoto...

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:05.300
What is this tawdry sob story?

00:13:05.940 --> 00:13:07.800
Are you Tokui-san?

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:09.760
So what if I am?

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:14.200
Yata-san told me that on top of 
trying to force her to drink,

00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:18.020
you got drunk and broke the restaurant's 
furnishings when you tripped.

00:13:23.470 --> 00:13:26.640
Th-This doesn't concern you! 
What are you even talking about?!

00:13:26.640 --> 00:13:27.490
Yeah!

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:31.200
Have some water.

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:35.270
What are you doing? That's dangerous!

00:13:35.270 --> 00:13:37.860
Looks like your arm doesn't hurt that bad.

00:13:39.350 --> 00:13:43.260
Are you sure you're not lying about 
both the violence and your injury?

00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:48.720
Who do you think you are?!

00:13:54.530 --> 00:13:56.140
What's this?

00:13:57.110 --> 00:14:00.400
I can't let my dad find out about this!

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:02.140
Who the hell was that guy?!

00:14:02.140 --> 00:14:04.360
I'm terribly sorry!

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:07.990
I actually have some reservations 
about Miyazumi, as well.

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:10.110
Do something about it, then.

00:14:10.110 --> 00:14:12.930
Actually, I have a suggestion.

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:20.000
How dare you drag me into this farce?

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:22.990
You won't get away with this!

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:27.220
No, wait!

00:14:27.650 --> 00:14:29.050
Sir!

00:14:31.740 --> 00:14:34.690
Oshitari-kun, for the time being...

00:14:35.240 --> 00:14:39.380
There seem to have been some factual 
errors concerning Vice President Tokui,

00:14:39.770 --> 00:14:43.860
but it's true that he enraged 
an important client!

00:14:44.100 --> 00:14:46.550
Allowing this man to be team captain

00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:49.330
and play his little badminton games

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:53.990
will bring down employee morale and 
negatively affect our business!

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:55.910
"Little badminton games"?

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:59.720
As far as serious, hardworking employees 
are concerned, it's just games.

00:14:59.720 --> 00:15:02.910
After all, you've failed to 
achieve anything significant.

00:15:02.910 --> 00:15:04.630
But we will!

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:07.010
We'll win the S/J League!

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:10.470
Oh? Let's make a bet, then.

00:15:10.690 --> 00:15:13.230
If you win, I'll overlook this incident.

00:15:13.230 --> 00:15:18.330
But if you lose, Miyazumi-kun 
will quit the team.

00:15:18.330 --> 00:15:20.480
What? What kind of deal is that?

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:22.930
Didn't you say you'd win?

00:15:22.930 --> 00:15:28.650
Or can't you? You're just a bunch 
of morons who are all talk!

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:30.230
Fine.

00:15:31.230 --> 00:15:33.620
We'll win the League.

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:36.700
Be as assertive as you want.

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:41.160
Your team may have lost already.

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:46.800
Damn it.

00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:49.760
Sorry, Bro. I'll get the next one.

00:15:50.530 --> 00:15:51.720
Sure.

00:15:59.820 --> 00:16:02.140
Is Toya out of gas?

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:09.690
<i>Crap, that was a weak shot!</i>

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:10.710
<i>Gotcha!</i>

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:12.490
<i>A cut smash!</i>

00:16:13.170 --> 00:16:14.450
<i>I won't make it in time!</i>

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:29.090
Nice cover!

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:31.950
<i>Sota-kun, you've changed.</i>

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:37.180
<i>You were scared of Toya-kun's expectations
 for you because you lacked self-confidence.</i>

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:38.470
<i>But now...</i>

00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:46.330
<i>Toya does what I can't, 
and I'll do what he can't.</i>

00:16:47.910 --> 00:16:54.190
<i>I'm not building ceilings and 
setting limits on myself anymore.</i>

00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:59.280
<i>I'll pour everything I've got 
into the things I can do!</i>

00:17:05.050 --> 00:17:06.540
That was awesome.

00:17:07.230 --> 00:17:08.920
I knew you could do it, Bro.

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:12.380
You're amazing, Bro!

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:18.990
Let your brother get the shots
 you can't reach, Toya.

00:17:22.190 --> 00:17:23.140
Got it!

00:17:24.050 --> 00:17:26.520
We're gonna win, Bro!

00:17:27.220 --> 00:17:29.780
You two seem rather close.

00:17:30.830 --> 00:17:32.940
<i>I'm gonna win, Bro.</i>

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:36.190
<i>Next time I'll take a game off you.</i>

00:17:34.980 --> 00:17:36.520
<i>You're too strong, Bro.</i>

00:17:36.520 --> 00:17:37.040
<i>Bro!</i>

00:17:37.040 --> 00:17:39.120
<i>You're really good at this, Bro.</i>

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:40.650
<i>I wanna beat you, Bro!</i>

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:44.250
You held back, didn't you, Bro?

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:49.400
<i>No. I played my best and lost.</i>

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:52.960
Are you really moving out?

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:56.120
Yeah. I want to focus on badminton.

00:18:00.580 --> 00:18:01.300
Hayato!

00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:06.520
19 all.

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:07.980
All right!

00:18:09.180 --> 00:18:10.650
<i>What obnoxious brothers.</i>

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:27.790
I returned your smash, Bro!

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:29.710
When are you gonna play me next?

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:31.750
You'd better go all-out next time.

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:32.670
Bro!

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:33.550
<i>Shut up!</i>

00:18:36.470 --> 00:18:38.540
Huh? Wasn't that...

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:50.650
What's wrong, Hayato? This isn't like you.

00:18:52.190 --> 00:18:53.150
Sorry.

00:18:58.220 --> 00:18:59.360
<i>Hang in there.</i>

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:02.990
<i>I can't keep relying on my brother.</i>

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:07.000
<i>Doubles is a two-player game, after all!</i>

00:19:07.610 --> 00:19:12.060
<i>Toya, you've worked harder than 
anyone else because you're so small.</i>

00:19:12.920 --> 00:19:16.500
<i>My hands were full managing my own problems,</i>

00:19:15.860 --> 00:19:17.440
<b>Gokura Kotetsu 
Saruhashi Yukei</b>

00:19:15.860 --> 00:19:17.440
<b>Takeda Koki 
Saeki Toya</b>

00:19:16.980 --> 00:19:20.130
<b>Yagami Jun 
Natsuki Ryo</b>

00:19:16.980 --> 00:19:20.130
<b>Takeda Koki 
Saeki Toya</b>

00:19:17.300 --> 00:19:19.560
<i>so I couldn't make the most of your efforts.</i>

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:25.720
<i>But with Sota, you should 
be able to go even higher.</i>

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:29.680
<i>I'll make this shot!</i>

00:19:29.960 --> 00:19:31.850
Go, Toya!

00:19:38.890 --> 00:19:41.950
<i>Please... let it fall!</i>

00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:44.120
<i>Not happening!</i>

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:51.000
<i>What?</i>

00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:10.480
Game and match won by Saeki Sota and 
Saeki Toya of Sunlight Beverage.

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:12.230
Yeah!

00:20:15.600 --> 00:20:17.570
Nice game!

00:20:23.330 --> 00:20:26.410
We did it, Bro. I knew you could do it.

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:31.000
I couldn't have done it without you, Toya.

00:22:16.270 --> 00:22:17.440
Miyazumi-san!

00:22:21.460 --> 00:22:22.590
How's the match going?

00:22:30.910 --> 00:22:34.660
<b>Misora Ayato</b>

00:22:30.910 --> 00:22:34.660
<b>Usuyama Toru</b>

00:22:35.120 --> 00:22:36.750
All right!

00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:38.270
Good job, guys!

00:22:39.660 --> 00:22:40.880
Miyazumi-san.

00:22:41.210 --> 00:22:44.340
You two are late as hell. 
What have you been doing?

00:22:44.340 --> 00:22:46.820
Sorry. We had some stuff to deal with.

00:22:47.810 --> 00:22:49.550
It's time.

00:22:50.290 --> 00:22:51.060
Yeah.

00:22:53.660 --> 00:23:00.250
<b>Sunlight Beverage</b>

00:22:54.280 --> 00:23:00.250
<b>Unisics</b>

00:22:54.910 --> 00:23:00.250
<b>Tomari Transport</b>

00:22:55.160 --> 00:23:00.250
<b>Mitsuhoshi Bank</b>

00:22:55.370 --> 00:23:00.250
<b>S/J League Finals
 Mitsuhoshi Bank vs. Sunlight Beverage</b>
